---
import Image from "astro/components/Image.astro";
---

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <article
      class="bg-[linear-gradient(45deg,#F8FDFF,#FFFFFF)] text-black rounded-2xl p-4 lg:p-10 border-2 border-main-200"
    >
      <h2 class="text-center">
        <span
          class="bg-linear-to-r from-[#0179B4] to-[#88D8FF] bg-clip-text text-transparent"
          >Who we are:
        </span> an operator, not an agency
      </h2>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[1fr_2fr] gap-4 lg:gap-10 mt-4 lg:mt-10 items-stretch text-center md:text-left">
        <div>
          <Image
            src="/img/img2.webp"
            alt="Illustrative reference image"
            format="webp"
            quality="low"
            width="448"
            height="344"
            class="w-auto h-auto mx-auto rounded-xl object-cover"
          />
        </div>
        <div class="h-full flex flex-col justify-between align-start">
          <p class="mb-5">
            For 18 years MedicSupport Network has built and operated hospitals and clinics across
            Africa and Asia. We started with a single facility in Ghana. We now operate
            18 across six countries, and the clinicians who staff them are people we employ and
            train rather than people we source.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-5">
            That distinction matters. Hospitals in Europe and America are short of nurses, midwives
            and paramedics, and the clinicians we place with them already work in our own licensed
            facilities, already hold current registration, and already answer to our standards. We
            are not an intermediary introducing strangers. We are sending our own people, and we
            stand behind them.
          </p>
          <a
            href="/about"
            class="btn bg-[linear-gradient(125deg,var(--color-main-100),var(--color-main-200))] text-white border-0 rounded-xl text-lg py-3 px-6 h-auto shadow-xl hover:shadow-2xl md:mr-auto"
            >About the group</a
          >
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
